      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there any point in retrying if the response is not correct?  Specifically, once the ROM/loader returns 0x80 in the response, seems like you can stop.\n\nAlso, I see that on failures, the expected response length is 6 bytes (command + status + crc32).  Flushing the input buffer seems like a good idea.\n\n```\nrf_cont_disp \u003d uart_handle.read(RESPONSE_LENGTH)\nif len(rf_cont_disp) \u003d\u003d 0:\n    # retry logic...\n    continue\n    \nif rf_cont_disp !\u003d resp_bytes:\n    # log error\n    uart_handle.reset_input_buffer()\n    sys.exit(1)\n    \noffset \u003d offset + program_length\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 133,
        "endChar": 38
      },
